    "result_text": "The build is green. The full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`, including the new `errorRejectsFutureDate` case) passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of a future `registrationDate` on `POST /api/owners`, following the existing `InvalidPostcode` validation pattern in this OfficeFloor function-injection codebase:\n\n1. **New step function** \u2014 `RequireCurrentRegistrationDate.java`: reads the bound request via `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` and, *when present*, throws if `registrationDate` is after `LocalDate.now()`. An absent date is left alone (server defaults it later), preserving the existing contract. It runs before `ApplyRegistrationDate`/`RequireDailyCapacity` so the raw supplied date is checked before any business-day roll-forward.\n\n2. **Checked escalation** \u2014 `FutureRegistrationDateException.java` (extends `Exception`, so it lands in the `throws` clause).\n\n3. **Handler** \u2014 `FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler.java`: responds `400` with body `{\"errors\":[\"registrationDate\"]}`, mirroring the postcode handler.\n\n4. **Escalation wiring** \u2014 `officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.FutureRegistrationDateException.yml`.\n\n5. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted the step into `owners.POST.yml` right after `require` (which republishes the body as a `@Val` variable) and before the normalization steps.\n\nNo `@RestController`/`@ControllerAdvice` was used \u2014 errors are thrown by functions and answered by an escalation handler, per the project conventions.",
